 🚀 Recommended Deployment Strategy

 Phase 1: Free Tier Testing (Oracle Cloud)

   1. Create Oracle Cloud Free Account
     • Go to https://www.oracle.com/cloud/free/
     • Sign up with your email
     • Get 4 ARM cores, 24GB RAM, 200GB storage
   2. Deploy Your Bot


 
   # SSH into your Oracle Cloud instance
   ssh ubuntu@your-oracle-ip
 
   # Clone your repository
   git clone your-repo-url
   cd aegis_quant
 
   # Install Python and dependencies
   sudo apt update
   sudo apt install python3 python3-pip python3-venv -y
 
   # Create virtual environment
   python3 -m venv .venv
   source .venv/bin/activate
 
   # Install dependencies
   cd server
   pip install -r requirements.txt
 
   # Configure .env file
   cp .env.example .env
   nano .env  # Add your MT5 credentials and API keys
 

   3. Configure MT5 Bridge


 
   # Install mt5linux
   pip install mt5linux
 
   # Configure your MT5 bridge connection
   # You'll need either:
   # - A Windows VPS with MT5 terminal
   # - A service that provides MT5 access
   # - Local MT5 terminal with port forwarding
 

 Phase 2: Production (Google Cloud or DigitalOcean)

 After successful testing, upgrade to:

   • Google Cloud: Use your $300 credit for high-performance Intel/AMD instances
   • DigitalOcean: $5-10/month for consistent performance

