 📋 Step-by-Step Deployment Guide

 For Oracle Cloud Free Tier:

   1. Create Oracle Cloud Account
     • Visit https://www.oracle.com/cloud/free/
     • Sign up and create your account
     • Create a compute instance (ARM architecture)
   2. Setup Your Instance


 
   # SSH into your instance
   ssh ubuntu@your-public-ip
 
   # Update system
   sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
 
   # Install Python and dependencies
   sudo apt install python3 python3-pip python3-venv git -y
 
   # Clone your repository
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/aegis_quant.git
   cd aegis_quant/server
 
   # Create virtual environment
   python3 -m venv .venv
   source .venv/bin/activate
 
   # Install dependencies
   pip install -r requirements.txt
 

   3. Configure Your Bot


 
   # Copy example .env file
   cp .env.example .env
 
   # Edit configuration
   nano .env
   # Add your MT5 credentials, API keys, etc.
 

   4. Install MT5 Linux Bridge


 
   # Install mt5linux
   pip install mt5linux
 
   # Enable it in config
   # Add to .env: MT5LINUX_ENABLED=1
 

   5. Run Your Bot


 
   # Start the bot
   python main.py
 

 For DigitalOcean ($5/month):

   1. Create DigitalOcean Account
     • Go to https://www.digitalocean.com/
     • Sign up and add payment method ($5)
     • Create a droplet (Ubuntu 22.04, 2GB RAM, 1 CPU, $5/month)
   2. Follow same setup as Oracle Cloud
     • The process is identical after SSH access

